.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt BIO_F_PREFIX 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BIO_f_prefix ,
.Nm BIO_set_prefix ,
.Nm BIO_set_indent ,
.Nm BIO_get_indent
.Nd prefix BIO filter
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/bio.h
.Ft const BIO_METHOD *
.Fo BIO_f_prefix
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft long
.Fo BIO_set_prefix
.Fa "BIO *b"
.Fa "const char *prefix"
.Fc
.Ft long
.Fo BIO_set_indent
.Fa "BIO *b"
.Fa "long indent"
.Fc
.Ft long
.Fo BIO_get_indent
.Fa "BIO *b"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr BIO_f_cipher 3
returns the prefix BIO method.
This is a filter for text output, where each line gets automatically
prefixed and indented according to user input.
.Pp
The prefix and the indentation are combined.
For each line of output going through this filter, the prefix is output
first, then the amount of additional spaces indicated by the
indentation, and then the line itself.
.Pp
By default, there is no prefix, and indentation is set to 0.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_set_prefix
sets the prefix to be used for future lines of text, using
.Fa prefix .
.Fa prefix
may be NULL, signifying that there should be no prefix.
If
.Fa prefix
isn't NULL, this function makes a copy of it.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_set_indent
sets the indentation to be used for future lines of text, using
.Fa indent .
Negative values are not allowed.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_get_indent
gets the current indentation.
.Sh NOTES
.Fn BIO_set_prefix ,
.Fn BIO_set_indent
and
.Fn BIO_get_indent
are implemented as macros.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn BIO_f_prefix
returns the prefix BIO method.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_set_prefix
returns 1 if the prefix was correctly set, or <=0 on failure.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_set_indent
returns 1 if the prefix was correctly set, or <=0 on failure.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_get_indent
returns the current indentation, or a negative value for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bio 7
